# Individual <%= Basket.model_name.human %> Modifications Preserved

When you edit a single <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> to deviate from the membership configuration (a different depot, a different <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, an adjusted quantity, custom <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>, or a swap to another delivery), these modifications are now **preserved** when the membership configuration changes later.

Until now, changing a membership's configuration (<%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, depot, delivery cycle, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>, ...) would destroy and recreate all future <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>, silently wiping out any per-<%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> customization you had set up. That's no longer the case.

On the membership page, any <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> that diverges from the membership configuration shows a small **history icon** next to its state. Hovering over the icon reveals who made the change and when, along with the list of modified fields. From there, an **"Undo"** button restores the <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> to the membership defaults.

A few things to keep in mind:

- **Member depot changes** from the member area are also captured (if allowed in [the membership update settings](/settings#membership_updates)), so switching the main depot of the membership won't override what a member picked for a specific <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %>.
- **<%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2) %> shifts** (from absences) keep working alongside these modifications. A <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> can both receive a shift and have a manual quantity adjustment without double-counting.
- If you later change the membership configuration to match a previously modified <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %>, the modification becomes a no-op and the icon disappears.

Find more information about this feature in [the deliveries handbook](/handbook/deliveries#basket-overrides).

Don't hesitate to [let me know](/support) if anything looks off on your existing memberships!
